 removed_case_id  warren diane p 63 f  reg ref 07 10    removed_case_id   wic kahan morton g  m d                                                                                             specimen   removed_accession_id   removed_case_id  sout received  07 10 06  removed_case_id  spec type    clinical diagnosis   history  hypoechoic mass  upper outer quadrant  left breast in patient with remote history of breast carcinoma with breast conserving therapy  hematoma  rule out carcinoma edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat mckj gross description  the specimen is received in one formalin container labelled  guided breast biopsy  left breast  3 o clock  and consists of five  soft  yellowish red  glistening needle biopsies ranging in size from 0 6cm  in length to 0 1cm  in diameter to 2 0cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter  5x all  dictated by  lv edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat mckj diagnosis  left breast  upper outer quadrant  needle biopsy  atypical cellular spindle cell proliferation with frequent mitoses and areas of necrosis  see note  edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat gild removed_date    removed_case_id  md fraje removed_date    removed_case_id  md fraje descriptive comment  note  immunohistochemical staining reveals positive reactivity to  removed_accession_id  and vimentin and no reactivity to actin  c kit  cytokeratin  desmin  factor viii  myosin  or  removed_accession_id   this pattern favors a mesenchymal rather than an epithelial phenotype  no associated invasive or in situ conventional breast carcinoma is seen  however  given the patient s history of a prior metaplastic  spindle cell or sarcomatoid  breast carcinoma   removed_accession_id    a diagnosis of recurrent or de novo metaplastic carcinoma must be considered  the differential diagnosis also includes malignant phyllodes tumor  postirradiation sarcoma  or other stromal sarcoma  a benign pseudosarcomatous process such as nodular fasciitis is deemed less likely  