sed of atypical spindle cells arranged in interlacing bundles  many contain mitotic figures and the cells in the center have undergone necrosis and hemorrhage  like you  i favor the diagnosis of malignancy  but i cannot distinguish between a spindle cell carcinoma  a high grade phyllodes tumor  and a stromal sarcoma based on this material  the possibility of nodular fasciitis seems unlikely because of the absence of a significant inflammatory infiltrate and the pronounced mitotic activity  it seems clear that the patient will have to undergo a complete excision of the mass to permit you to reach a definite diagnosis  final diagnosis  breast  left   core biopsy  malignant tumor composed of spindle cells  see note  addendum report  continued  note  diagnostic possibilities include sarcoma  phyllodes tumor  and spindle cell carcinoma  addendum final  fraser jean l  md      removed_date  07 19 06  removed_case_id   by md fraje addendum  1 entered  07 17 06  removed_case_id      additional diagnostic information     this report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing additional diagnostic information  the original diagnosis is unchanged  immunohistochemical studies performed on the formalin fixed  paraffin embedded block reveal the following results for the tumor cells  estrogen receptor  negative  antibody  6 removed_accession_id   detection system  avidin biotin complex  progesterone receptor  negative  antibody  pgr 1 removed_accession_id   detection system  avidin biotin complex   removed_accession_id  neu  c erb  removed_accession_id    negative for overexpression  antibody   removed_accession_id   detection system  avidin biotin complex addendum final  fraser jean l  md      removed_date  07 17 06  removed_case_id   by md fraje edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord removed_date    removed_case_id  md fraje removed_date    removed_case_id  pat gild removed_date    removed_case_id  md frajecodes   removed_accession_id    breas