accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  finaltype  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  18 aug 03 accessioned on  18 aug 03 at 13 28 clinical data  ultrasound core biopsy of abnormal intramammary lymph node                                                                                      final diagnosis     breast  right  1 o clock   core biopsies  lymphoid tissue with features of reactive hyperplasia with kappa immunoglobulin light chain excess  see note   note  the large core biopsies show lymphoid tissue with some appreciable lymph node architecture  there are several reactive germinal centers  the interfollicular region contains predominantly small lymphocytes with scattered immunoblasts and plasma cells  immunoperoxidase stains  see addendum  show b cells   removed_accession_id    predominantly confined to follicles with no abnormal antigen expression  there is an excess of igm kappa positive plasma cells  but lambda positive cells are also present  this finding raises the possibility of early involvement by lymphoplasmacytic lymphoma or marginal zone lymphoma  overall  i favor a reactive process  however  to exclude low grade lymphoma  excision of the lymph node would be helpful if clinically indicated  diagnosis by  nancy lee harris  m d  signed on  21 aug 03 at 17 47                                                                                     immunohistochemistry addendum     results of immunoperoxidase stains  on paraffin sections  with antibodies to immunoglobulin light chains  kappa  lambda  there is polytypic staining of scattered plasma cells in a diffuse pattern with slight excess of kapppa  with antibody to immunoglobulin heavy chain  mu  there is staining of many scattered plasma cells in a high background staining  with antibodies to b lineage antigen s    removed_accession_id   there is staining of many cells in a follicular pattern  the b cells are negative for antibody to  removed_accession_id  and cyclin  removed_accession_id    removed_accession_id  stain showed many follicular dendritic meshworks  many of which are expanded  the follicles are positive for  removed_accession_id  and  removed_accession_id  and negative for  removed_accession_id   with antibodies to t lineage associated antigen s    removed_accession_id    removed_accession_id    there is staining of many small cells in the interfollicular region  with antibody to  removed_accession_id   many scattered immunoblasts and plasma cells are stained  the cells are negative for  removed_accession_id   together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results do not establish a definite diagnosis  and cannot rule out a b cell lymphoma  see note  note  these tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the pathology department at the massachusetts general hospital  they have not been cleared or approved by the u s  food and drug administration  fda   the fda has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  added by  nancy lee harris  m d  signed on  22 aug 03 at 18 03 gross description  received in formalin   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name and unit number only  are four cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from removed_date x 0 2cm to removed_date x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette a  gross description by  julie zwirble resident  paul n  staats  md                                                                                 source care unit  mgh outpatient  off p clinic  reports to  kevin s  hughes  m d  isaac schiff  m d  dianne georgian smith  m d  kenneth lloyd minaker  m d  part   breast  right 1 00   core biopsy , benign.
